# Strategic Priorities Analysis Workflow
# Leverages full system: HTN + Graph + Morphism Transformations + Team Routing
#
# This workflow will be:
# 1. Compiled to HTN (hierarchical task network)
# 2. Optimized via morphism transformations (flatten, simplify, remove identity)
# 3. Converted to dependency graph (DAG validation)
# 4. Executed with team-based routing
#
# Flow: Parallel analysis → Sequential evaluation → Synthesis

# Phase 1: Parallel deep analysis (product operator ×)
# Each analysis runs independently
functor sprint4_analysis = Analyze Sprint 4 completion: morphism transformations, 732 tests passing, property-based testing with Hypothesis. Identify technical debt, follow-up opportunities, and integration points with existing HTN/Graph systems.

functor architecture_analysis = Review current architecture: DSL parser, HTN compiler, Graph validator, Dynamic executor pool, Morphism transformations, MorphismWorkflowExecutor. Identify gaps, bottlenecks, extension points, and scaling concerns.

functor roadmap_analysis = Analyze README roadmap and git history: Phase 2 items (OpenAI SDK handoffs, guardrails), future enhancements (Claude provider, observability, web UI). Which align with our category theory foundation?

functor test_analysis = Deep dive into test coverage: 95% with 732 tests, property-based tests with Hypothesis. Which critical paths lack coverage? What edge cases are missing? Where do we need more integration tests?

# Parallel execution (4 analyses run concurrently)
functor parallel_analysis = sprint4_analysis x architecture_analysis x roadmap_analysis x test_analysis

# Phase 2: Sequential strategic evaluation (composition operator ∘)
# Each evaluation builds on previous results
functor debt_evaluation = Evaluate technical debt vs new features based on all analyses. What MUST be addressed before production? What refactoring is critical? What can be deferred?

functor category_evaluation = Sprint 4 delivered morphisms and property tests. Evaluate next steps in category theory: Natural transformations between functors? State monads for stateful workflows? Adjunctions? Provide cost-benefit analysis with effort estimates.

functor production_evaluation = Assess production readiness gaps: monitoring, error handling, performance optimization, documentation, deployment automation. What's blocking real-world usage?

# Sequential composition (each builds on previous)
functor sequential_evaluation = production_evaluation o category_evaluation o debt_evaluation

# Phase 3: Full pipeline composition
# Evaluation depends on analysis completing first
functor evaluation_pipeline = sequential_evaluation o parallel_analysis

# Phase 4: Strategic synthesis
functor strategic_synthesis = Generate TOP 5 prioritized sprint recommendations based on all analysis and evaluation. For each sprint provide: 1) Sprint name and clear goal, 2) Detailed task breakdown (3-5 tasks), 3) Effort estimate (hours/days), 4) ROI analysis (business value vs implementation cost), 5) Dependencies and risks, 6) Success metrics and acceptance criteria. Format as actionable sprint plans ready for immediate implementation.

# Main workflow: Full pipeline
# This will be:
# - Compiled to HTN (hierarchical decomposition)
# - Optimized via morphisms (flatten compositions, remove identities, simplify structure)
# - Validated as DAG (cycle detection)
# - Executed with team routing
functor main = strategic_synthesis o evaluation_pipeline
